  "body": "<p>The rivalry between Aryna Sabalenka and Iga Swiatek could resume at the Dongfeng • Voyah Wuhan Open. The two former World No. 1s were draw together in the first quarter of the last WTA 1000 event of the season on Saturday, an event that Sabalenka has won three times.</p>\n<p>Following the pre-tournament withdrawals of World No. 1 Elena Rybakina and defending champion Coco Gauff, Sabalenka will look to win her first tournament since March as the top seed. Jessica Pegula, last year's finalist, is seeded No. 2. Mirra Andreeva and Linda Noskova, both of whom officially qualified for the year-end WTA Finals Indian Wells due to results at the ongoing China Open, are the No. 3 and No. 4 seeds.</p>\n<p>Here is a quarter-by-quarter breakdown of the draw, including first-round matches to watch and potential quarterfinal matchups.</p>\n<p>To see the full draw, <a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/tournaments/wuhan-open/draws\">click here</a>. </p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n</div><h4>First quarter</h4>\n<h5>First-round match to keep an eye on </h5>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://www.wtatennis.com/players/328120/qinwen-zheng\" data-tracking=\"true\" data-tracking-event=\"click_track\" data-tracking-component=\"link click\" data-tracking-category=\"content\" data-tracking-type=\"news\" data-tracking-detail=\"Zheng Qinwen \" data-tracking-widget-type=\"Article Widget\" data-tracking-widget-name=\"Article Page Widget\">Zheng Qinwen</a> vs. Ann Li</strong>: 2024 Olympic champion Zheng has experienced a home-soil resurgence this week at the China Open on her way to the final. Regardless of her upcoming result against Mirra Andreeva, she'll hope to continue her momentum in Wuhan, where she reached the final in 2024.</p>\n<p>There, she lost to Sabalenka -- the opponent for the winner between Zheng and American Li, who upset Belinda Bencic to reach the third round in Beijing.</p>\n<p><strong>Additional first-round matches: </strong>Janice Tjen vs. Oleksandra Oliynikova, [14] Elise Mertens vs. Daria Snigur, [9] Belinda Bencic vs. Zhang Shuai, Diane Parry vs. Anna Kalinskaya, Qualifier vs. Qualifier</p>\n<h5>Potential quarterfinal showdown</h5>\n<p><strong>[1] Aryna Sabalenka vs. [7] Iga Swiatek: </strong>Sabalenka and Swiatek have met 13 times previously, but last dueled more than a year ago at Roland Garros. The two are in vastly different places than when they last met, with Sabalenka having surrendered her World No. 1 ranking to Rybakina and Swiatek fighting for a place in the year-end Top 8 -- making a potential reunion all the more interesting.</p>\n<p>Swiatek leads the overall head-to-head 8-5, but the two players have split six meetings all-time on hard courts. </p><div class=\"articleWidget center\">\n        <aside class=\"instagram-post embeddable-widget embeddable-widget--floating embeddable-widget--centered-mobile \"><blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DeR713inYuJ/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\" style=\" background:#FFF; border:0; border-radius:3px; box-shadow:0 0 1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.5),0 1px 10px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.15); margin: 1px; max-width:540px; min-width:326px; padding:0; width:99.375%; width:-webkit-calc(100% - 2px); width:calc(100% - 2px);\"><div style=\"padding:16px;\"> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DeR713inYuJ/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" style=\" background:#FFFFFF; line-height:0; padding:0 0; text-align:center; text-decoration:none; width:100%;\" target=\"_blank\"> <div style=\" display: flex; flex-direction: row; align-items: center;\"> <div style=\"background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 50%; flex-grow: 0; height: 40px; margin-right: 14px; width: 40px;\"></div> <div style=\"display: flex; flex-direction: column; flex-grow: 1; justify-content: center;\"> <div style=\" background-color: #F4F4F4; border-radius: 4px; flex-grow: 0; height: 14px; margin-bottom: 6